WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.291
- [Narrator] Here in the south of England,

00:00:02.291 --> 00:00:03.824
(whoosh)
behind these beach huts,

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:05.130
(whoosh)
is a very weird

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.560
and wonderful floating houseboat village.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Well, sometimes it floats,
and other times it sits on mud

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.190
because of the tide, but that
doesn't matter right now.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.630
So without further ado,

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.184
let's roll the title card.

00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:17.101
(ding)

00:00:39.582 --> 00:00:41.400
So, let's get to know Hamish.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.545
He has seven boats.

00:00:42.545 --> 00:00:43.980
(popping)

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.810
He has a microwave as a postbox.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.580
(lid shuts)

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.016
He can do this with a saw.

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:51.630
(slaps)
(high-pitched whir)

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.000
He has a grand collection of ...

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.563
Let's leave that there.

00:00:56.628 --> 00:00:58.170
(piano music)
Hamish moved here

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.903
32 years ago after falling on tough times.

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:33.312
Where on Earth do you get a
nose cone from a jumbo jet?

00:01:37.335 --> 00:01:38.663
(chuckles)
Fair enough.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.729
(sawing)

00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:48.828
(hammer bangs)

00:01:48.828 --> 00:01:50.243
Now, I know what you're thinking.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.840
Why on Earth is there a bus

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.049
or a scrap car on a boat?

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:56.299
(chuckles)

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.701
(chuckles)

00:02:12.141 --> 00:02:14.641
(light music)

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:23.626
(popping)

00:02:36.244 --> 00:02:38.411
(popping)

00:02:44.784 --> 00:02:46.867
(sawing)

00:02:51.226 --> 00:02:53.643
(light ding)

